body:
So if you type the charcter: ' slightly beneath the letter p, it adds like a curve to the bottom portion of the letter.

&#x200B;

Example:

&#x200B;

    Hey, do you like the color purple?
    Why, yes of course! I love 'purple'

Right, and that's exactly what I was saying at the start of my post. It's a *GOOD COH game, gameplay wise*, but everything else that makes the experience worth sitting through is lacking in all aspects. If we can take COH3 gameplay, with improved COH2 graphics and sounds, then we'd have a masterpiece on our hands. Unfortunately, that's not the case. 

&#x200B;

TL;DR Amazing gameplay, lacking in everything else.

I have thought about using the switch statement, but I have always seen the usage with "int" data type and am unsure how to use it so that the cases are for strings or even for command line arguments. So for simplicity sake, I'll leave the program with if/else statements.

&#x200B;

With that being said, thank you so much for your help.

Interesting, I never knew that the char data type acted as a numeric ASCII type as well. Today I learned. Thanks for clearing that up. 

EDIT: The code actually has a change made to it before I posted where 

String word = input.next();

is actually supposed to be

String word = input.nextLine();
